      "summary": "Record a bounded engineering decision for the neutral collection host, initially wrapping the retained Agent source cohort inside its existing module, with isolated Observer. Compare at most two concrete package/composition alternatives; proposed packages/collection-go versus application-owned effectful host. Choose a narrower scope, defer or reject with named owner/reviewer and reasons. Do not implement or decide every source at once.",
      "scope": "Map existing diskstats/network/SMART/platform/Observer acquisition boundaries to proposed interface symbols, effects, clocks/quality/budgets, connection/privilege/store/wire and consumers; pin source revision. Separate installed/available/authorized-enabled/entitled. Select module/import graph, compiled registration and one-release-manifest shape; keep core pure, source adapters independent and composition roots responsible. Wrap in Agent module first; one-read ZFS/TrueNAS parity and no cross-application internal imports. No arbitrary plugins, new probes, native listener choice or duplicated collections.",
      "done": "Complete JSON decision, readable rationale and independently authored fixture specification. Record selected/narrower/deferred/rejected disposition with actor/time/scope/artifact hash; proposed paths/symbols versus existing separate. If selected, create only a bounded host-contract/reference-build follow-on with exact files and synthetic inert source, then separately scoped retained-source migration and qualification tasks. No refactor occurs by closing this decision.",
